---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const title = 'Healthee — the health companion that refuses to flatter you';
const description =
  'Most fitness apps cheer you on no matter what. Healthee tells you the truth about your body, kindly — and says "I don\'t know yet" when it should. A companion for the Amazfit Helio Strap. Still being built.';
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <Nav />

  <main id="main">
    {/* 1 — The opening truth + the turn + the anchor */}
    <section class="moment" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h1 id="hero-title" class="say-huge rise">
          Every app tells you <span class="warm">&ldquo;great job.&rdquo;</span> Even when
          it isn&rsquo;t true.
        </h1>
        <p class="lede rise mt-8" style="max-width:38rem;">
          Healthee is the one that won&rsquo;t. It&rsquo;s a health companion that
          <strong style="color:var(--c-ink);font-weight:600;">refuses to flatter you</strong> —
          it tells you the truth about your body, kindly, and says &ldquo;I don&rsquo;t know
          yet&rdquo; when it really doesn&rsquo;t.
        </p>
        <p class="plain rise mt-6" style="max-width:38rem;">
          It works with a little fitness band you wear on your wrist. No cheering. No fake
          numbers. Just an honest read, and the next small thing worth trying.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    {/* 2 — One quiet moment of honesty (the rendered example) */}
    <section class="moment" aria-labelledby="honest-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="honest-title" class="say-big rise">
          Most days it has plenty to say. Some days it says <span class="warm">this</span>.
        </h2>
        <p class="lede rise mt-7">
          When the band hasn&rsquo;t seen enough of you, other apps guess anyway — a cheerful
          number that isn&rsquo;t really there. Healthee just tells you the truth:
        </p>

        <figure class="mt-8 rise" aria-label="An example of what Healthee says when it doesn't have enough data">
          <p class="aside mb-3">An example of what it says</p>
          <div class="quiet">
            <p class="voice">
              &ldquo;I don&rsquo;t have enough to score you today. Wear it tonight and
              I&rsquo;ll know more in the morning.&rdquo;
            </p>
          </div>
          <figcaption class="aside mt-3">
            &ldquo;Not enough to be sure&rdquo; always beats a guess that makes you feel good.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
    </section>

    {/* 3 — What it is: the band, free numbers, the paid coach (with a warm exchange) */}
    <section class="moment" aria-labelledby="what-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="what-title" class="say-big rise">
          A companion for a band you can buy <span class="warm">anywhere</span>.
        </h2>
        <p class="lede rise mt-7">
          Healthee works with the <strong style="color:var(--c-ink);font-weight:600;">Amazfit
          Helio Strap</strong> — a small, screenless band you can buy on your own, from anyone.
          We don&rsquo;t sell it and we&rsquo;re not part of the company that makes it. We just
          make it honest.
        </p>
        <p class="plain rise mt-6">
          Everything the band measures — your sleep, your heart, how rested you are — is
          <strong style="color:var(--c-ink);font-weight:600;">free, forever</strong>. The part
          you pay for is the coach: someone in your pocket who reads your numbers and talks to
          you plainly about them.
        </p>

        <figure class="mt-9 rise" aria-label="An example conversation with the Healthee coach">
          <p class="aside mb-3">An example conversation</p>
          <div class="quiet">
            <p class="voice"><span class="text-ink-faint">You:</span> Did I sleep okay?</p>
            <hr class="rule my-5" />
            <p class="voice">
              <span class="text-ink-faint">Healthee:</span> Not really. You were short by about
              an hour and a half, three nights running, and it&rsquo;s starting to show. Tonight,
              try heading to bed 30 minutes earlier — of everything you could change, that&rsquo;s
              the one most likely to help.
            </p>
          </div>
          <figcaption class="aside mt-3">
            Everything it tells you is backed by real research you can read yourself — or it
            doesn&rsquo;t say it.
          </figcaption>
        </figure>

        <p class="plain rise mt-9">
          The coach costs less than one coffee a month:
          <strong style="color:var(--c-ink);font-weight:600;">$3.99 a month, $34.99 a year, or
          $99 once</strong> (the one-time price is an early-supporter offer, while it lasts). For
          a sense of scale, other bands ask a lot more just to see your own numbers:
          <a class="u-link" href="https://www.whoop.com/us/en/membership/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Whoop</a>
          starts at $199 a year, and
          <a class="u-link" href="https://ouraring.com/membership" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Oura</a>
          is $69.99 a year on top of a $349 ring <span class="text-ink-faint">(prices from their
          own sites, July 2026)</span>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    {/* 4 — How you'll get it + the data promise */}
    <section class="moment" aria-labelledby="get-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="get-title" class="say-big rise">
          When it&rsquo;s ready, there&rsquo;ll be <span class="warm">two</span> honest ways to
          get it.
        </h2>

        <div class="mt-8 rise">
          <p class="voice" style="font-size:clamp(1.15rem,2.1vw,1.5rem);">We run it for you.</p>
          <p class="plain mt-2" style="max-width:40rem;">
            The simple way — you just use the app. This opens the moment the app is ready. It
            isn&rsquo;t yet, so there&rsquo;s nothing to sign up for today.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="mt-7 rise">
          <p class="voice" style="font-size:clamp(1.15rem,2.1vw,1.5rem);">You run it yourself.</p>
          <p class="plain mt-2" style="max-width:40rem;">
            The whole thing is yours to run on your own computer if you&rsquo;d rather. The code
            goes up on GitHub the moment it&rsquo;s ready to run yourself — and the link will
            appear right here.
          </p>
        </div>

        <hr class="rule-soft mt-10 rise" />

        <h3 class="voice rise mt-9" style="font-weight:600;">Your numbers stay yours.</h3>
        <ul class="mt-5 flex flex-col gap-3.5 rise" style="max-width:40rem;list-style:none;padding:0;">
          <li class="plain flex gap-3"><span class="warm" aria-hidden="true">&mdash;</span> Kept
            separate from everyone else&rsquo;s. Your data is never mixed in with other people&rsquo;s.</li>
          <li class="plain flex gap-3"><span class="warm" aria-hidden="true">&mdash;</span> Your
            password never touches us — signing in is handled somewhere safe, away from your health data.</li>
          <li class="plain flex gap-3"><span class="warm" aria-hidden="true">&mdash;</span> Backed
            up every night, so nothing gets lost.</li>
          <li class="plain flex gap-3"><span class="warm" aria-hidden="true">&mdash;</span> Never
            sold. And there are no trackers on this page — not even to count visitors.</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    {/* 5 — The honest goodbye */}
    <section class="moment" aria-labelledby="bye-title">
      <div class="wrap">
        <h2 id="bye-title" class="say-big rise">
          It won&rsquo;t pretend to be your <span class="warm">doctor</span>.
        </h2>
        <p class="lede rise mt-7" style="max-width:40rem;">
          Healthee isn&rsquo;t a medical device and it won&rsquo;t diagnose you. If something in
          your numbers looks worth worrying about, it&rsquo;ll say so plainly — and tell you to
          see a real doctor. That&rsquo;s the honest thing to do.
        </p>
        <p class="plain rise mt-8" style="max-width:40rem;">
          It&rsquo;s still being built, out in the open, one honest piece at a time. There&rsquo;s
          nothing to sign up for yet. When it&rsquo;s ready, this is where you&rsquo;ll find it.
          <strong style="color:var(--c-ink);font-weight:600;">Watch this space.</strong>
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <Footer />
</Base>
